	shorttitle = {Gravity {Inversion} for {Sub}-{Ice} {Shelf} {Bathymetry}},
	url = {https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15614239},
	abstract = {This Zenodo release contains all the materials related to the paper "Gravity Inversion for Sub-Ice Shelf Bathymetry: Strengths, Limitations, and Insights from Synthetic Modeling" accepted for publication at The Cryosphere. 

synthetic\_bathymetry\_inversion-0.1.0.zip

This contains an archive of the GitHub repository https://github.com/mdtanker/synthetic\_bathymetry\_inversion at the state when the paper was accepted for publication at The Cryosphere. The repository archived is version 0.1.0. All of the notebooks contained in the repository and associated documentation can be viewed at https://mdtanker.github.io/synthetic\_bathymetry\_inversion/

ice\_shelves.zip

The output from the antarctic ice shelf analysis portion of the work. For all Antarctic ice shelves, this zip contains:



{\textless}shelf-name{\textgreater}\_constraints.csv.gz: a CSV of existing point measurements of bathymetry/bed topography, computed here

{\textless}shelf-name{\textgreater}\_grav\_anomalies.csv.gz: a CSV of observed gravity data (AntGG-2021) and computed anomalies, computed here

{\textless}shelf-name{\textgreater}\_min\_dist.nc: a netCDF of a grid of distances to the nearest point measurement of bathymetry/bed topography, computed here

{\textless}shelf-name{\textgreater}\_constraints.png: a plot of the grid of distances to the nearest point measurement of bathymetry/bed topography, created here

{\textless}shelf-name{\textgreater}\_info.png: a plot of all the computed gravity anomaly grids and the nearest distance grid, created here


ice\_shelf\_gravity\_stats.csv: a single CSV (1 row per ice shelf) containing statistics of the gravity anomalies and the nearest distances grids, created here.

ice\_shelf\_gravity\_stats\_added\_constraints.csv: a single CSV (1 row per ice shelf) showing how the median constraint proximity values for a shelf change when a single additional constraint point is added to the location of maximum distance to the nearest constraint, created here.

antarctica\_constraints.csv.gz and antarctica\_constraints.parquet: all of the constraints from each ice shelf merged into one file, created here.

antarctica\_grav\_grids.nc: all the computed gravity anomalies from each shelf merged into one file, created here.

antarctica\_min\_dist.nc: all the computed grid of distances to the nearest point measurement of bathymetry/bed topography merged into one file, created here.

Ross\_Sea.zip

The output from running all the individual inversions (1-5) and the inversion ensembles (1-4). 

ice\_shelf\_stats.csv

A CSV with 1 row per ice shelf giving the computed statistics regarding constraint proximity and gravity anomalies, and the predicted optimal gravity inversion RMSE and topography improvement (relative to Bedmap2), as shown here.},
